1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
This is Supper Club AI: one agent-readable workspace
for a complete cultural gathering.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:17,760
We open thesupperclub dot app inside ChatGPT.
The page registers its own WebMCP tools.

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:29,320
One brief turns Toni Morrison's Jazz into a Harlem supper for eight—
with budget, dietary needs, and wine carried into the plan.

4
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:38,500
Spoonacular supplied three live courses. GrapeMinds curated wine.
Perplexity discovered the soundtrack, and Apple Music verified it.

5
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:45,110
Every source and fallback stays visible.

6
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:51,800
The host can change one decision
without rebuilding the evening.

7
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:58,240
ChatGPT searches gluten-free mains, prices exact candidates at a selected
Kroger location, then replaces only the host's choice.

8
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:20,010
That one change flows downstream: ingredients regroup by dish and aisle,
the prep timeline rebuilds, and source-aware recipe cards scale each dish.

9
00:01:26,330 --> 00:01:31,500
With a real store selected, Kroger estimates the local basket
and reports match coverage, promotions, and confidence—

10
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:36,010
without pretending every ingredient matched.

11
00:01:39,130 --> 00:01:49,770
GrapeMinds pairings, Apple Music artwork and previews, cultural notes,
and Agent Marginalia stay inspectable beside the shared plan.

12
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:04,900
The agent stops at consequential actions.

13
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:12,770
Only after explicit host approval does WebMCP finalize the plan
and download a kitchen packet with recipe cards and provenance.

14
00:02:23,900 --> 00:02:34,380
For wine shops and independent grocers, this same plan can become
a guided storefront experience—local, useful, and always host-controlled.
